            <div xml:id="d48">

                <pb facs="0157" n="63" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg63"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 296/658a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-10-14T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 14,
                                1924—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>332. For Logan. L–132. French Embassy has communicated informally following
                    message received from French Government: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The British Government proposed to the interested Governments the date
                            of October 14th for the meeting of the Experts to have charge to study
                            the repartition of payments according to the Dawes Plan. The French
                            Government found that date too near in order to be able to collect the
                            necessary information for the discussion, so <pb facs="0158" n="64"
                                xml:id="pg64"/> the French Government proposed that the date of the
                            meeting be postponed to October 27th.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Please repeat to London as Department’s 363 for information only.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
